<title>UK: Cadbury hit by Coca-Cola results.</title>
<headline>Cadbury hit by Coca-Cola results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Cadbury Schweppes Plc fell 6-1/2 pence to 526-1/2 after a good set of Coca-Cola results, analysts said.</p>
<p>Strong growth for Coca-Cola could mean loss of market share for Cadbury's Dr Pepper/Seven Up unit, they added.</p>
<p>Coca-Cola Co on Monday reported a 38 percent jump in first-quarter profits.</p>
<p>The results included an unexpectedly strong nine percent gain in domestic unit sales, giving Coke its best result in the mature U.S. market in 11 years.</p>
<p>&quot;Cadbury could be struggling against those kind of figures,&quot; said one analyst.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
